   "section": "hook",
   "overlays": {
    "hook": "He spied on the British, *and stayed enslaved.*"
   },
   "captions": false,
   "speed": 1.45
  },
  {
   "id": "name",
   "text": "This is James Lafayette.",
   "visual": {
    "kind": "title",
    "title": "James Lafayette",
    "sub": "about 1748 to 1830"
   },
   "section": "who"
  },
  {
   "id": "spy",
   "text": "In 1781, enslaved in Virginia, he went to serve the Marquis de Lafayette as a spy, and slipped into the British camp again and again.",
   "visual": {
    "kind": "card",
    "image": "lafayette82",
    "caption": "The Marquis de Lafayette, 1782"
   },
   "section": "story",
   "overlays": {
    "stamp": "1781"
   }
  },
  {
   "id": "york",
   "text": "Lafayette learned that Cornwallis had moved his army to Yorktown. There, he was trapped.",
   "visual": {
    "kind": "card",
    "image": "yorkplan",
    "caption": "Yorktown, 1781"
   }
  },
  {
   "id": "surr",
   "text": "On October 19, 1781, Cornwallis surrendered.",
   "visual": {
    "kind": "card",
    "image": "surrender",
    "caption": "The Surrender of Lord Cornwallis, by John Trumbull"
   }
  },
  {
   "id": "law",
   "text": "But Virginia freed enslaved men who had served as soldiers. James had been a spy. He stayed enslaved.",
   "visual": {
    "kind": "title",
    "title": "Still enslaved",
    "sub": "after the war"
   },
   "section": "twist"
  },
  {
   "id": "cert",
   "text": "So Lafayette wrote for him. His intelligences from the enemy's camp were industriously collected, and most faithfully delivered.",
   "visual": {
    "kind": "card",
    "image": "cert",
    "caption": "Lafayette's certificate, 1784"
   }
  },
  {
   "id": "free",
   "text": "On January 9, 1787, Virginia set him free. He took the name Lafayette.",
   "visual": {
    "kind": "card",
    "image": "james",
    "caption": "James Lafayette, 1824"
   },
   "section": "legacy"
  },
  {
   "id": "hug",
   "text": "In 1824, the old general saw him in a crowd, called him by name, and embraced him.",
   "visual": {
    "kind": "card",
    "image": "lafayette25",
    "caption": "The Marquis de Lafayette, 1825"
   }
  },
  {
   "id": "end",
   "text": "He helped win the war, and then had to win his own freedom.",
   "visual": {
    "kind": "photo",
    "image": "james",
